       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "ARF w mod–severe carditis:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " oral prednisone instead of ASA (⍉data that adding it in minimal–mild carditis helps). ⍉suppressed after 2 days, or severe HF: IV methylprednisolone 30 mg/kg QD (max 1 g/day) x3D may be given. Oral course typically 2–4 wk, then taper over 2–3 wk; start ASA during the taper."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Contraindicated in systemic fungal infect. ⍉live vaccines @ immunosuppressive doses. Caution: HF, HTN, renal insuff; peptic ulcer, diverticulitis (perf risk)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "CYP3A4 inducers (phenytoin, carbamazepine, RIF, barbiturates) may require a higher steroid dose; inhibitors (ketoconazole, itraconazole, ritonavir, erythromycin) raise levels. NSAIDs/ASA: ↑ GI SE. Warfarin: response USU inhibited; monitor INR often. K-depleting diuretics: watch for hypokalemia."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Watch for infect. Long-term:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " consider osteoporosis prev (calcium, vitD, bisphos, weight-bearing exercise); use the lowest effective dose and duration."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
